{"author":{"id":"fd8b9fbee3ca9e1e8bc93ac1e52482b167d597d9903cceb294967fa0f6114e08"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786490213,"nonce":"TR6bUYZlg+A4aYu++Vjg+AjSEXo=","message":"Fixed by `HudFixSystem` (`src/HudFix.h/cpp`), and written up as game_defects_notes.md 12.\n\n**What it does.** Detours `RenderHudItems` @ 0x0055fb20, calls the original, then flushes the\nimmediate 2D batch and opens a fresh one while `Camera_Hud` is still current. The meter and icon\nquads then go out under viewport 0.03..0.04 and clamp to their authored 0.03 - the front of the\nHUD slice, which is where they were always meant to be - instead of clamping up to 0.1 under the\nworld viewport.\n\n**It splits the batch rather than re-pointing the flush, and that is the whole design.**\n`DrawOrderMenu` appends one more bar to the same batch (`Hud2D_DrawMeterBar` @ 0x0049b322) at\nz = 0.1f, authored for `Camera_World` - it is a unit health bar over the world, not a panel\nelement. One flush is one DrawIndexedPrimitive under one viewport, so forcing `Camera_Hud` over\nthe whole thing would have dragged that bar from 0.1 to clamp(0.1, 0.03, 0.04) = 0.04 and moved a\nsecond thing while fixing the first. End/Draw/Begin mid-batch is a transition the engine already\nperforms itself when the vertex buffer fills (`Hud2D_DrawQuad` @ 0x005695e6).\n\n**Two things that make the seam safe, both measured.** `RenderHudItems` has exactly one call site\n(0x0046e8c1) and **zero** literal occurrences of its address in .text/.rdata/.data under an\nunaligned byte-by-byte scan - so it is in no vtable and no callback table, and it is always\nreached inside an open `Hud2D_BeginBatch` window on both branches of `RunInGameFrame`.\n`Hud2D_FlushBatch` is the same: one call site, no literal references. An empty batch costs a\nlock/unlock pair and nothing else, because `RenderBatch_Draw` opens with `CMP [ESI+0x50],0`.\n\n**Verified in the running game**, level02, camera settled and paused:\n\n- the meters and both item icons render, under **both** `GKPLUS_RENDERER=d3d8` and\n  `GKPLUS_RENDERER=vulkan`, identically;\n- draw 65 moved from `0.1000..1.0000` to `0.0299..0.0399` in `render.frame_draws`, and no second\n  batch draw appeared - `DrawOrderMenu` contributed nothing that frame, so its fresh batch\n  short-circuited exactly as designed;\n- **nothing else in the frame changed.** Per-region against the pre-fix capture: HUD panel MAD\n  1.985, top HUD strip **0.0000 (0 of 19,800 pixels differ)**, world upper-left **0.0000 (0 of\n  1,120,000)**. The only other differences are the two units at a different animation phase and\n  the objectives text at a different point in its fade, i.e. the cross-launch drift\n  vulkan_renderer_notes.md 4.30 names;\n- `render.validation` empty, every \"must be 0\" counter 0, 9 pipelines.\n- `GKPLUS_HUD_FIX=raw` restores the stock behaviour - re-shot and confirmed identical to the\n  original empty troughs.\n\n**Also landed, from what the investigation turned up:**\n\n- rendering_notes.md **4.4** - new: 2D layer order is a camera per depth slice, the nine cameras\n  and their ranges, the canonical four-step camera switch, and the fact that every camera ZFUNC is\n  `D3DCMP_LESSEQUAL` so ties go to the later draw. Also corrects two labels in 3 and 4.1\n  (`FUN_005695a0` was called \"in-game menu\"; it opens the immediate 2D batch).\n- vulkan_renderer_notes.md **4.45** now carries a correction: its \"the panel that should cover it\n  wins\" read this same bar as correct reference behaviour. The clamp rule and every measurement\n  there stand; only that sentence was wrong.\n- address_map.md - the HUD 2D functions, the camera viewport/depth API, and the nine camera\n  globals with their slices.\n- **src/Camera.h was wrong about the object it mirrors.** It claimed \"the engines object is\n  0x23e bytes\"; the base `Camera` is **0x26c** and the derived `CameraData` **0x2a0**, from\n  `CameraData_Ctor` @ 0x004b0190 - which has no xrefs at all, being reached from a CRT\n  static-initialiser table sitting as undefined bytes. `CameraCoords` @ 0x007b4e0c is\n  `CameraData + 0x26c`, a **member**, not the separate global this repo treated it as. The mirror\n  now asserts 0x2a0 and records the layout, including the `D3DVIEWPORT8` at +0x254 that all of the\n  above depends on.\n- Renames mirrored into the notes: `DrawHud` -\u003e `HudItem_DrawByKind` (it draws one item, dispatched\n  on kind - the old name described the caller), `FUN_0055fb20` -\u003e `RenderHudItems`,\n  `FUN_0056a7b0` -\u003e `HudItem_Draw`, `FUN_005695a0` -\u003e `Hud2D_BeginBatch`,\n  `FUN_004af4d0` -\u003e `InitRenderCameras`.\n\nOne thing deliberately left open, recorded in game_defects_notes.md 12: because ZFUNC is\n`LESSEQUAL`, a plate whose NDC z were exactly 0 would tie at 0.03 and, drawn later, still win. It\nevidently is not - the meters render - but the margin is unmeasured. If this ever flickers, the\ntie-proof variant is a degenerate viewport range (cam+0x264 = cam+0x268 = 0.029f) for the batch\ndraw only; `Camera_UpdateDepthState` rewrites both from +0x19c/+0x1a0 on the next change, so a\nmissed restore self-heals.\n\nChanges are in the working tree, uncommitted. Bug refs are local until `git bug push origin`.","files":null}]}